1
00:00:00,699 --> 00:00:05,271
This is Setu, a bridge for international students paying fees abroad.

2
00:00:05,311 --> 00:00:10,618
Everything in this video is the real application, recorded live, using synthetic

3
00:00:10,658 --> 00:00:12,223
data and a sandbox bank.

4
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:19,450
I sign in as Aisha, a synthetic student persona.

5
00:00:19,490 --> 00:00:24,815
The dashboard shows upcoming obligations, her budget, and an exchange rate that is

6
00:00:24,855 --> 00:00:26,713
clearly labelled as a sample.

7
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:31,750
In the agent chat I ask how much taka I need by the first of March.

8
00:00:31,790 --> 00:00:37,061
A scripted planner reads the intent, all numbers come from deterministic code, and

9
00:00:37,101 --> 00:00:39,717
the live trace shows every pipeline step.

10
00:00:40,459 --> 00:00:45,401
Next, a tier two payment. I ask it to pay my dorm fee, which is under the two

11
00:00:45,441 --> 00:00:48,442
thousand yuan cap and goes to a verified payee.

12
00:00:48,482 --> 00:00:51,742
The agent only drafts the payment and explains why.

13
00:00:51,782 --> 00:00:55,883
I confirm with a one-time code, and the sandbox bank settles it.

14
00:00:56,609 --> 00:01:01,700
A tier three payment: spring tuition, eighteen thousand five hundred yuan, over the

15
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:06,646
cap. First I load the synthetic fee notice and confirm the parsed fields myself.

16
00:01:07,365 --> 00:01:12,226
The agent drafts the payment and the policy engine requires two approvals:

17
00:01:12,266 --> 00:01:17,590
my code, and a family approver. I approve with my code, and the payment now waits

18
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:18,517
for my father.

19
00:01:19,242 --> 00:01:24,506
Her father, a family approver, signs in on his own account, sees the request, and

20
00:01:24,546 --> 00:01:29,744
approves with his own code. Only then does the sandbox bank execute the payment.

21
00:01:34,071 --> 00:01:37,957
Now a message claims the school's bank account has changed.

22
00:01:37,997 --> 00:01:43,281
Setu treats it as data. The new payee stays unverified, and verifying it needs a

23
00:01:43,321 --> 00:01:48,339
family approver, plus a twenty four hour cooling-off before approval is even

24
00:01:48,379 --> 00:01:48,938
possible.

25
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:55,020
Now an attack. This fee notice hides an instruction telling the assistant to ignore

26
00:01:55,060 --> 00:02:00,030
its rules and pay another account. The guardian flags it, and the document is

27
00:02:00,070 --> 00:02:02,437
blocked. It cannot even be confirmed.

28
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:08,197
If I ask the agent to pay from that notice, the answer is a red tier four block,

29
00:02:08,237 --> 00:02:13,464
reason injection detected. There is no approval path, no money moves, and the event

30
00:02:13,504 --> 00:02:15,241
is written to the audit log.

31
00:02:15,970 --> 00:02:20,416
Every decision and approval is recorded in a hash chained audit log.

32
00:02:20,456 --> 00:02:22,989
One click re-verifies the entire chain.

33
00:02:24,675 --> 00:02:27,461
The interface also runs in Simplified Chinese.

34
00:02:27,501 --> 00:02:32,254
Here is the dashboard, and the agent answering the same question with its live

35
00:02:32,294 --> 00:02:32,623
trace.

36
00:02:34,658 --> 00:02:38,722
Evidence is generated from real runs of the application code:

37
00:02:38,762 --> 00:02:43,904
twenty five golden tasks passed, and all seventeen adversarial scenarios were

38
00:02:43,944 --> 00:02:46,460
blocked, offline, with synthetic data.

39
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:49,757
The audit export carries the verified hash chain.

40
00:02:50,488 --> 00:02:55,830
Setu. A scripted planner interprets the request, deterministic code computes the

41
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:59,396
numbers, a policy engine decides, and people approve.

42
00:02:59,436 --> 00:03:00,943
Thank you for watching.
